---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Experience from '../components/cv/Experience.astro';
import Section from '../components/cv/Section.astro';
import Skill from '../components/cv/Skill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/paths';
import '@fontsource-variable/figtree';
import {
  EMAIL,
  GITHUB_URL,
  LINKEDIN_URL,
  SITE_TITLE,
  SITE_URL,
} from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="Ed Jex CV" description="Ed Jex's CV">
  <main class="page post">
    <div class="row screen-only">
      <nav class="main post-nav">
        <a href={sitePath('/')}>{SITE_TITLE}</a>
        <a href={sitePath('/cv.pdf')}>PDF</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
    <div id="cv">
      <header>
        <h1>Edward Jex</h1>
        <ul>
          <li>{EMAIL}</li>
          <li><a href={SITE_URL}>edjex.dev</a></li>
          <li><a href={GITHUB_URL}>github.com/Jex-y</a></li>
          <li><a href={LINKEDIN_URL}>linkedin.com/in/ed-jex</a></li>
        </ul>
      </header>
      <div class="columns">
        <p class="summary">
          MEng Computer Science, Durham 2025, top of the year. I build small,
          efficient models: a 12,387-weight detector that runs on 2.2 µJ a
          frame, 680× less than YOLO11-nano; a 227k-parameter model that reads
          strikethrough in patent amendments at 3 ms a line on CPU; and a
          diffusion model in under a million parameters. At <a
            href="https://solveintelligence.com">Solve Intelligence (YC S23)</a
          >, a fast-moving legal AI startup, I also rebuilt the agent loop as a
          service that runs thousands of LLM agents in the background. My
          research interests are mechanistic interpretability and reinforcement
          learning.
        </p>
        <div class="column primary">
          <Section title="Experience">
            <Experience
              title="Software Engineer"
              subtitle="Solve Intelligence (YC S23)"
              date="July 2025–present"
            >
              <ul>
                <li>
                  Rewrote the core agent loop as its own microservice, out of
                  the API. Agents now run in the background for hours, survive
                  deployments, and scale to thousands at once. Results stream
                  over Redis and server-sent events to the frontend, where they
                  trigger actions; a reconnecting client resumes from a cursor
                  with no gaps or duplicates.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Took Charts from prototype to a production product used by
                  thousands of customers, working end to end: the agent loop and
                  AI tools, a planner delegating to subagents, through to the
                  rich-text, cell-based editor. Tens of hours of attorney work
                  now take minutes.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Scaled agents from short, bounded tasks to long, open-ended
                  ones: lazy document loading and parallel OCR for time to first
                  token, and hunting down GIL-bound work to fit many agents on
                  one container.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Shipped across the stack: Postgres row-level security, live
                  sharing, and patent language and jurisdiction conversion.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Trained a 227,746-parameter (834 KB) model that labels each
                  OCR character as struck or underlined, at 3 ms a line on two
                  CPU threads, replacing image tokens at a sixth of the context
                  cost. Took it apart with a pre-registered, 76-run retraining
                  ablation: a placebo set the noise floor at a quarter of a
                  point, and removing a part and retraining cost far less than
                  switching it off (3.7 points against 94).
                </li>
              </ul>
            </Experience>
          </Section>
          <Section title="Research and projects">
            <Experience
              title="Energy-efficient object detection on edge devices"
              subtitle="MEng thesis, supervised by Dr Farshad Arvin"
            >
              <p>
                Asked how little energy a useful detector can spend. Treated
                detection as one heatmap peak per animal rather than boxes,
                trained five hundred architectures across a GPU cluster and
                measured each on a Hailo-8L, because architecture explained only
                15% of the variance in energy on the accelerator (80% on CPU).
                The best has three layers and 12,387 weights, reaching
                <strong>0.948 AP</strong> at <strong
                  >2.2 µJ a frame, 680× less than YOLO11-nano</strong
                >. It runs in the browser on hand-written WGSL compute shaders,
                with every layer's feature maps inspectable.
              </p>
              <p class="links">
                <a href="https://edjex.dev/blog/final-year-project/">write-up</a
                > · <a
                  href="https://github.com/Jex-y/lpcv-project-implementation"
                  >code</a
                >
              </p>
            </Experience>
            <Experience
              title="Deep learning under a parameter budget"
              date="Module 90%, 2024"
            >
              <p>
                A class-conditional diffusion model with classifier-free
                guidance in under a million parameters, reaching
                <strong>FID 18.1</strong> on CIFAR-100, and a 100k-parameter MobileNetV3
                variant with grouped pointwise convolutions.
              </p>
            </Experience>
            <Experience
              title="Sample-efficient RL for BipedalWalker"
              date="Module 90%, 2024"
            >
              <p>
                Compared four model-free methods, then extended TD-MPC2 to solve
                BipedalWalker in under 100 episodes.
              </p>
            </Experience>
            <Experience
              title="Temporally consistent video translation"
              date="Module 75%, 2025"
            >
              <p>
                A UVCGAN2-style ViT-UNet CycleGAN, extended with MoCycle-GAN
                motion losses from RAFT optical flow, trained on an A100.
              </p>
            </Experience>
          </Section>
        </div>
        <div class="column secondary">
          <Section title="Education">
            <Experience
              title="Durham University"
              subtitle="MEng Computer Science, First Class"
              date="2021–2025"
            >
              <p>
                81% four-year average, 86% in the final year; prizes for the top
                project (91%) and the top overall grade. Data Compression 93%,
                Quantum Computing 89%, Advanced Algorithms 88%.
              </p>
            </Experience>
            <Experience title="A Levels: 4 A*s" date="2021">
              <p>Maths, Further Maths, Physics, Computer Science.</p>
            </Experience>
          </Section>
          <Section title="Skills">
            <Skill
              name="Machine learning"
              subskills={[
                'Hardware-aware NAS, quantisation, energy measurement',
                'Edge deployment: ONNX, Hailo, WebGPU',
                'PyTorch, JAX, Flax; GPU clusters',
                'CNNs, transformers, diffusion, GANs',
                'RL: TD-MPC2, SAC, REDQ, DropQ, CrossQ; MCTS',
              ]}
            />
            <Skill
              name="Engineering"
              subskills={[
                'Python, Rust, TypeScript, C/C++',
                'Production LLM agents: orchestration, tool use, streaming',
                'Postgres, Redis, Celery, FastAPI, React',
                'AWS, GCP, Docker, CI/CD',
              ]}
            />
          </Section>
          <Section title="Other experience">
            <Experience
              title="Web Development Intern"
              subtitle="Cisco, Webex web client"
              date="Summer 2022"
            >
              <p>
                Rich message rendering, build system migration, React and Redux
                UI components.
              </p>
            </Experience>
            <Experience
              title="Teaching Assistant"
              subtitle="Durham Computer Science"
              date="2023–2025"
            >
              <p>
                Ran labs for Computational Thinking and Networks and Systems.
              </p>
            </Experience>
            <Experience title="River level forecasting" date="2024">
              <p>
                PyTorch forecast served from Rust with ONNX Runtime, used by
                Durham rowing clubs. <a href="https://river.edjex.dev"
                  >river.edjex.dev</a
                >
              </p>
            </Experience>
            <Experience
              title="President"
              subtitle="Trevelyan College Boat Club"
              date="2023–2024"
            >
              <p>
                Ran finances, training and racing; replaced ageing equipment and
                grew the membership.
              </p>
            </Experience>
          </Section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Fraunces CV';
    font-weight: 300;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('../fonts/fraunces-300.woff2') format('woff2');
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Fraunces CV';
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('../fonts/fraunces-400.woff2') format('woff2');
  }

  #cv {
    --accent: #35573f;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.6mm;
    width: min(210mm, 100% - 2 * var(--pad));
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-family: 'Figtree Variable', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  #cv :global(p) {
    font-size: inherit;
    line-height: inherit;
  }

  #cv :global(a) {
    text-decoration-thickness: 0.5pt;
    text-underline-offset: 1.5pt;
  }

  #cv :global(h2) {
    padding-bottom: 0.8mm;
    border-bottom: 0.5pt solid var(--accent);
    font-family: 'Fraunces CV', Georgia, serif;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 1.38em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  #cv :global(.subtitle) {
    font-style: normal;
  }

  header {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 3mm 8mm;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: 'Fraunces CV', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 4.8em;
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  header ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3mm;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--note);
  }

  .summary {
    font-size: 1.07em;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .links {
    color: var(--note);
  }

  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3.7mm 8mm;
  }

  .column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.7mm;
  }

  @media print, (min-width: 820px) {
    #cv {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      width: 210mm;
      min-height: 297mm;
      padding: 10.6mm 11.6mm;
      outline: 1px solid var(--tool-light);
      font-size: 9.1pt;
    }

    header ul {
      text-align: right;
    }

    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 56.6mm;
      grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;
      grid-template-areas: 'summary secondary' 'primary secondary';
    }

    .summary {
      grid-area: summary;
    }

    .primary {
      grid-area: primary;
    }

    .secondary {
      grid-area: secondary;
    }
  }

  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media print {
    main {
      padding: 0;
    }

    .screen-only {
      display: none;
    }

    #cv {
      height: 297mm;
      outline: none;
    }
  }
</style>
